## Overview

Today I learned how to extract multiple pieces of information through a single visible column during a UNION-based SQL Injection attack.

## Challenge

The application only displayed one column of output, making it impossible to display usernames and passwords separately.

## Solution

Used PostgreSQL string concatenation to combine multiple values into a single output column.

## Payload

' UNION SELECT NULL,username||':'||password FROM users--

## Example Output

administrator:password123

## Key Lesson

Attackers often need to adapt their payloads to application constraints. When only one column is visible, multiple values can be merged into a single output field and still be extracted successfully.
